  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Sixteen thousand Californians were ordered out in hours. What fed this fire?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "The Norte Fire started Friday morning in San Clemente, Orange County, officials say. It crossed into San Juan Capistrano. The fire authority reports about five hundred seventy acres burned, and at least six homes damaged or destroyed."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Santa Ana winds are hot, dry gusts blowing from inland toward the coast. Fox Weather calls this the first such wind event of the season. The fire authority says evacuation orders cover about forty-six hundred homes and sixteen thousand people."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Two firefighters were hospitalized and are stable, officials say. As of Saturday morning, the fire was five percent contained. The cause is under investigation. Other fires broke out around Los Angeles during the same wind event. Officials say the figures are preliminary and may change."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will crews fully contain the Norte Fire by Wednesday? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
